64 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 44 0 R
/E (4. Create a Dashboard page and add four chart widgets sourced from the same form: a bar chart comparing booking counts across Processing_Department and Age, a pie chart showing the distribution of Preferred_Room_Type choices, a bar chart plotting Preferred_Checkin_Date against Guest_Requests_Notes, and a radar chart summarising total bookings by Preferred_Checkin_Date.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
65 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 44 0 R
/E (The Hotel_Booking_Form built in Experiment 4 now captures every new booking request in a structured record, but the front office and management still have no consolidated way to review this data. Scanning submissions one record at a time makes it difficult to see how many bookings are sitting with each department, which room types are most in demand, how booking volume is spread across upcoming check-in dates, or which special requests guests most commonly report.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [14]
>>
